{
  "id": "bigville_cemetery",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R53 (block 364000): the CHURCHYARD CEMETERY, FUNERALS, and the PAUPER'S GRAVE -- where the dead go, as an economic event (the death-end parallel to where rubbish goes). The cemetery is AT THE CHURCH (church -has_cemetery-> cem). cy_funeral: a death with a SOLVENT estate (estate >= church.funeral_fee) gets a church FUNERAL -- the estate PAYS the fee (church revenue, coin conserved) and the UNDERTAKER digs a proper grave. cy_pauper: an estate that CANNOT pay gets a PAUPER'S GRAVE (pauper=1, no fee, the parish bears it, no funeral) -- the poverty gradient reaches the grave. cy_unburied_hazard: no undertaker -> the body lies unburied (a hazard, like unmanaged rubbish). In a SMALL TOWN the undertaker is ALSO the DOCTOR -- one person holds BOTH roles (a PLURAL office; bigville_office's one-office-per-person is a big-town assumption). Composes with the church (funerals, like services/counsel; funeral fees = church income), the map (the churchyard is by the church), bigville_office (death VACATES the deceased's posts -> succession; the undertaker is an appointed role), the doctor, ownership/estate (the estate pays), and the health/poverty line.",
  "nodes": [],
  "edges": [],
  "productions": [],
  "concepts": [],
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "cy_funeral",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "A death with a SOLVENT estate (estate >= church.funeral_fee): the CHURCH holds a funeral in the CHURCHYARD -- the estate PAYS the fee (church.coin += fee, estate -= fee, coin conserved), the UNDERTAKER digs a proper Grave (pauper=0), the body is buried. Funeral fees are church revenue.",
